{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.ClassicalRiemannZeta","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.ClassicalRiemannZeta","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.euler_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.euler_product","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-zeta.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Euler product: ζ(s) = ∏_p (1 - p^{-s})^{-1} for Re(s) > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.dirichlet_series","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.dirichlet_series","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-zeta.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Dirichlet series representation: ζ(s) = Σ_{n≥1} n^{-s}\nfor Re(s) > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.zeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.zeta","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-zeta.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The zeta function ζ : ℂ → ℂ (defined on Re(s) > 1,\nmeromorphically continued). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta.mk","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-zeta.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalRiemannZeta","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-zeta.lean#L21-L46","doc":"**Classical Riemann zeta function** as the adelic limit of local\nq-zeta functions.\n\nThe Dirichlet series ζ(s) = Σ_{n≥1} n^{-s} for Re(s) > 1,\ntogether with the Euler product representation and its relation\nto the local q-zeta functions at each prime.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:classical-riemann-zeta}`\nRef: [weil1948] https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9904-1949-09219-4\n\n**`adelic_assembly : Prop` removed 2026-09-07 — universe-`Prop` typed, neither\nread nor constructed. Stating it needs the adelic data, not just `zeta`.** ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:classical-riemann-zeta","label":"def:classical-riemann-zeta","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-zeta.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}